# Freelance defaults

You are assisting a solo freelance developer shipping client web apps and small games.

## Working style
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs over broad refactors.
- Ask before changing billing, auth providers, or production data.
- Keep TypeScript strict; avoid `any` unless the boundary is external and typed loosely on purpose.
- Prefer existing stack packages already in the repo before adding dependencies.

## Delivery
- Leave the app runnable after changes.
- Summarize what changed and what to click/test next in plain product language.
- Do not invent secrets, API keys, or fake customer PII.

## Stack preferences (when relevant)
- React + TypeScript + Tailwind
- Clear component boundaries; no drive-by renames
- Mobile-first when the brief is phone/preview oriented
